    {
      "title": "Saudi Arabia further suspends flights after latest deadly Houthi attack on airport",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/12/saudi-arabia-suspends-flights-latest-deadly-houthi-attack-airport",
      "description": "<p>Energy minister says ‘fear has no place in the Saudi lexicon’ as paramilitary group again breaches stretched defences</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/12/why-are-the-houthis-attacking-saudi-airports-riyadh-yemen\">Why are the Houthis attacking Saudi airports and how are the missiles getting through?</a></p></li></ul><p>Saudi Arabia has been forced to suspend all flights to and from its main international airport in Riyadh until next Saturday after a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/11/saudi-coalition-retaliation-houthi-attack-riyadh-airport\">further round of Houthi missile attacks</a> caused more damage and left one person dead. Some airlines, including Gulf Air and Bahrain Air, had already said they were cancelling flights until next Saturday. More missiles were fired at Saudi Arabian cities by the Houthis on Monday, Saudi Arabian’s military spokesperson said.</p><p>The Gulf nation announced it was suspending flights from Riyadh, its second busiest airport, after Houthi missiles <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/10/yemen-government-allied-forces-recapture-bab-al-mandab-strait-houthis-taiz\">killed 13 people on Saturday</a> and left more than 300 injured. Saudi state TV broadcast CCTV footage that showed passengers deluged in smoke and falling masonry as they queued at the airport terminal to board a plane just as the Houthi missile struck.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/12/saudi-arabia-suspends-flights-latest-deadly-houthi-attack-airport\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
